Security: Fix PostgreSQL tenant connection leak via auth_utils

The previous change introduced a critical IDOR vulnerability by
scoping `set_config` for `app.current_tenant` to the session instead
of the transaction. This patch reverts the `auth_utils.rs` `set_config`
third argument back to `true` (transaction-scoped) and securely fixes
the `revoke_token` vulnerability by checking `is_multitenant_mode` and
`should_bypass` when performing garbage collection sweeps on tokens.
